{"title":"2018 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of four consecutive odd integers is 200. What is the largest of these four integers?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the largest number of the four integers. Since the four numbers are all consecutive odd numbers, the other numbers must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41be156ba98071197428779c0cdc7ab3510fc51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 6$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1ca8117ac830f6274ce78b701a94c7269ec449b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ffc131d8b736f8faba00e9c6227958a93e76cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 2$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>The sum is then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/697325b2093faa807f79407f7a86846f6f64b802.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 6 + x - 4 + x - 2 + x = 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"256\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef0056216d7ae357fd378f423be8e1062daafa09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x - 12 = 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79caa8ff60714110a402d476f3bd858c53047766.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x = 200 + 12 = 212$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"165\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f57fbb9045e937ed209756fc75c81e6810e1c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{212}{4} = \\boxed{53}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2018 CEMC CTMC\">2018 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2018 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2018 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_2\" title=\"2018 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 2\">Team Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2018 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Team Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>